{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"efad694d2cb905e551200a3538007bb069ab797daed4d4468636128ac1390c0e","slug":"jupyter-optional-features","location":"/92-jupyter-optional-features/jupyter-optional-features.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Jupyter Optional Features","authors":[{"id":"Johan Mabille (@JohanMabille)","name":"Johan Mabille (@JohanMabille)"}],"date":"2023-06-26","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/blob/main/92-jupyter-optional-features/jupyter-optional-features.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jupyter/enhancement-proposals/edit/main/92-jupyter-optional-features/jupyter-optional-features.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"jupyter-optional-features.md","url":"/enhancement-proposals/build/jupyter-optional-fea-a62f3ed40d4d73def0c71cbdad83d81f.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"LzpIkyjc2g"}],"identifier":"summary","label":"Summary","html_id":"summary","implicit":true,"key":"tge1wO9BZ5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This JEP introduces Jupyter optional features, which ease the way\na kernel advertises which features it supports, without coupling it\nto the version of the protocol that it implements.","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"UkH84tgbSL"}],"key":"OVotPpBnLU"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Motivation","position":{"start":{"line":21,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"key":"rw02mm77Yt"}],"identifier":"motivation","label":"Motivation","html_id":"motivation","implicit":true,"key":"GicjGemlGQ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some of the features that were added (the debugger) or proposed (the subshells)\nmay require a lot of work from kernel authors to implement. Besides, the\nchanges they introduce on the protocol are self-contained; it is possible for a\nkernel to not support them without altering its exepected behavior regarding the\nrest of the protocol, and it is easy for a client to enable or disable such a\nfeature as long as it knows whether the kernel supports it. By the way, the\ndebugger is already optional, although it does not explicitly state it.","position":{"start":{"line":23,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"key":"hwFjUwDEqG"}],"key":"DzYKCNeK2F"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal of this JEP is to introduce the notion of optional features in the protocol\nand to have an explicit list of such features. This way, we do not prevent kernel\nauthors from upgrading to a more recent version of the protocol when we introduce\na new feature that may be complicated to implement and not mandatory for them.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"KEhjeaBrBs"}],"key":"x8cxGmB7DB"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Proposed Enhancement","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"gdW5xlGsy2"}],"identifier":"proposed-enhancement","label":"Proposed Enhancement","html_id":"proposed-enhancement","implicit":true,"key":"lzxesYHndT"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We propose to add a new ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"HLRLc0WUHQ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supported_features","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"lIV5xNBUrd"},{"type":"text","value":" field to the ","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"iYTaA7OvIb"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kernel_info_reply","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"ycVUwEUkD1"},{"type":"text","value":" message.\nThis field is a list of optional features that the kernel supports. The boolean field\n","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"XAiTQF99ts"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debugger","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"ijIvMBSZyl"},{"type":"text","value":" should be deprecated, as it would duplicate a possible value of the list.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"REyunoRzhI"}],"key":"kcZv7VTLaS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An optional feature can be a list of additional messages and/or a list of additional\nfields in different existing messages. When a feature introduces new messages, it is\nits responsibility to specify the order of these messages when it makes sense. Under\nno circumstances this feature should alter the order of already existing messages,\nnor interleave new messages between already existing messages.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"lkhRIOrHm7"}],"key":"pVHOAF4rWK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The documentation should indicate which optional feature a message (or a field of a\nmessage) is linked to when it is relevant. This would ease the implementation of\nnew kernels and the upgrade to new versions of the protocol.","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"e7vQq7hBrk"}],"key":"dC5VVE4V6B"}],"key":"d7o4Oo3Yus"}],"key":"YvPY8omd12"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Jupyter kernel subshells","url":"/kernel-subshells","group":"JEPs"},"next":{"title":"Debugger support to `copyToGlobals`","url":"/debugger-info-copy-to-globals","group":"JEPs"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}